{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1095 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "e92f6788fe3269bdb86e64530ae15f5e7d29530dbfbc3b1aad085f5934ba4734" :edb/db-before-t 1094 :edb/db-after-t 1095 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534407 50 #inst "2026-10-07T00:50:08.949Z" 13194139534407 true] [17592186100802 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286714 13194139534407 true] [17592186100802 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286723 13194139534407 true] [17592186100803 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286700 13194139534407 true] [17592186100803 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286707 13194139534407 true] [17592186100803 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286720 13194139534407 true] [17592186286700 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286701 13194139534407 true] [17592186286700 1089 "q-102680" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286700 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534407 true] [17592186286700 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-5,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286700 1113 #uuid "41593654-f415-5a2c-93db-d22404043236" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286700 1145 "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=x \\\\ y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-5\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=y+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Pythagorean identity ${sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t=1$, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+(y+5)^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is ${x}^{2}+(y+5)^{2}=1.$" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286702 13194139534407 true] [17592186286701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286703 13194139534407 true] [17592186286701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286704 13194139534407 true] [17592186286701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286705 13194139534407 true] [17592186286701 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286706 13194139534407 true] [17592186286701 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534407 true] [17592186286701 1041 "selection" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286701 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286706 13194139534407 true] [17592186286701 1110 #uuid "180c32c0-795e-5515-966d-d76b773245f2" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286702 1034 "{x}^{2}+(y-5)^{2}=1" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286702 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534407 true] [17592186286702 1111 #uuid "13b6bf5f-de6b-5a75-bf93-405ff7c79895" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286703 1034 "{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}=1" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286703 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534407 true] [17592186286703 1111 #uuid "4d4ce40a-c8bd-52a9-8ca1-6ba24cc7a091" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286704 1034 "(x+5)^{2}+(y+5)^{2}=1" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286704 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534407 true] [17592186286704 1111 #uuid "e13fb946-64a9-5a65-a92c-0dd7d3de3fc6" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286705 1034 "(x-5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286705 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534407 true] [17592186286705 1111 #uuid "9aec7d39-e939-5b26-b10f-fad087549190" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286706 1034 "{x}^{2}+(y+5)^{2}=1" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286706 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534407 true] [17592186286706 1111 #uuid "9e275085-0e4a-5583-b791-c7e2baf6af2b" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286707 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286708 13194139534407 true] [17592186286707 1089 "q-24574" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286707 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534407 true] [17592186286707 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as \n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286707 1113 #uuid "36736bcd-efb2-5212-8d19-2e9566214f4e" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286707 1145 "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=\\frac{x}{4} \\\\ y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using double angle formula for cosine and the Pythagorean identity, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-(1-{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}⁡t-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=\\frac{x}{4}$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{2}$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{2} & =2{(\\frac{x}{4})}^{2}-1 \\\\ \\frac{y}{2} & =2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16})-1 \\\\ \\frac{y}{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-1 \\\\ y & =2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-1).$" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286709 13194139534407 true] [17592186286708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286710 13194139534407 true] [17592186286708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286711 13194139534407 true] [17592186286708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286712 13194139534407 true] [17592186286708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286713 13194139534407 true] [17592186286708 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534407 true] [17592186286708 1041 "selection" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286708 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286709 13194139534407 true] [17592186286708 1110 #uuid "b21508f7-2e05-50c0-b19d-eab2a3362502" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286709 1034 "y=2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-1)" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286709 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534407 true] [17592186286709 1111 #uuid "7b94afa7-6522-56a9-8927-f7dac1bbe5b9" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286710 1034 "y=3{x}^{2}+8" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286710 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534407 true] [17592186286710 1111 #uuid "b53b3003-8098-5f2f-93a2-c103ed233318" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286711 1034 "y=3(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}-1)" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286711 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534407 true] [17592186286711 1111 #uuid "0ed902b0-8898-5dc9-a5da-1ed11561e15c" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286712 1034 "y=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286712 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534407 true] [17592186286712 1111 #uuid "7fb3e46b-f073-5209-9715-96ae750ab40c" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286713 1034 "y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+1" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286713 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534407 true] [17592186286713 1111 #uuid "43d6b6b9-93e2-537d-bf57-ea07b8468064" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286714 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286715 13194139534407 true] [17592186286714 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286718 13194139534407 true] [17592186286714 1089 "q-276284" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286714 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534407 true] [17592186286714 1100 "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{t-4},\\,\\,\\,y=\\frac{t}{2t+1},\\,t\\ne 4,\\,\\,\\,t\\ne -\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,x\\ne $\n{{field-2}}$,\\,\\,\\,x\\ne 0.$" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286714 1113 #uuid "309c7d82-5c17-5c66-8c6c-ddd74fbd88e2" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286714 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for $t:$\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{t-4}\\,⇒\\,t=\\frac{4x+1}{x}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=\\frac{4x+1}{x}$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{(\\frac{4x+1}{x})}{(2\\cdot \\frac{4x+1}{x}+1)} \\\\ y & =\\frac{(\\frac{4x+1}{x})}{(\\frac{8x+2}{x}+1)} \\\\ y & =\\frac{(\\frac{4x+1}{x})}{(\\frac{9x+2}{x})} \\\\ y & =\\frac{4x+1}{\\cancel{x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{x}}{9x+2} \\\\ y & =\\frac{4x+1}{9x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=\\frac{4x+1}{9x+2}.$\n\nFinally, since $t\\ne -\\frac{1}{2}$ and $x=\\frac{1}{t-4}$ has range $x\\ne 0,$ we must have \n$x\\ne -\\frac{2}{9},\\text{ }0.$ \n\nTherefore, the complete Cartesian equation is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{4x+1}{9x+2},\\,x\\ne -\\frac{2}{9},\\,\\,\\,x\\ne 0.\n$$" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286716 13194139534407 true] [17592186286715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286717 13194139534407 true] [17592186286715 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534407 true] [17592186286715 1041 "field-1" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286715 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286716 13194139534407 true] [17592186286715 1110 #uuid "cfd2ab57-be77-5f98-8816-290151d70b69" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286716 1034 "\\frac{4x+1}{9x+2}" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286716 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534407 true] [17592186286716 1111 #uuid "7e0bedc1-52d5-552e-81e6-98df7a8ff781" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286717 1034 "\\frac{4x+1}{9x+3}" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286717 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534407 true] [17592186286717 1111 #uuid "a320e021-72c0-5a3a-9617-98e85e4d657a" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286718 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286719 13194139534407 true] [17592186286718 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534407 true] [17592186286718 1041 "field-2" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286718 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286719 13194139534407 true] [17592186286718 1110 #uuid "d0e3dbbf-5944-520f-916c-a305e73a1f18" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286719 1034 "-\\frac{2}{9}" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286719 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534407 true] [17592186286719 1111 #uuid "99eab99a-56a7-5bc4-8e46-c52757fda0f3" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286720 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286721 13194139534407 true] [17592186286720 1089 "q-321314" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286720 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534407 true] [17592186286720 1100 "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534407 true] [17592186286720 1113 #uuid "04d0e7b2-dd26-589b-9743-7a5468d31ccf" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286720 1145 "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=\\frac{x}{5} \\\\ y=-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=-\\frac{y}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the double-angle formula for cosine and the Pythagorean identity, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-(1-{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}⁡t-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=\\frac{x}{5}$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=-\\frac{y}{6}$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{y}{6} & =2{(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}-1 \\\\ -\\frac{y}{6} & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{25}-1 \\\\ y & =-6(\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{25}-1) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{12{x}^{2}}{25}+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=-\\frac{12{x}^{2}}{25}+6.$" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286721 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286722 13194139534407 true] [17592186286721 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534407 true] [17592186286721 1041 "field-1" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286721 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286722 13194139534407 true] [17592186286721 1110 #uuid "8ae8d1d6-e209-5b42-8fa4-9c8a3205eef6" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286722 1034 "6-\\frac{12}{25}x^2" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286722 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534407 true] [17592186286722 1111 #uuid "9058db1a-9c53-57f5-944d-c26c19fe507b" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286723 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286724 13194139534407 true] [17592186286723 1089 "q-6830" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286723 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534407 true] [17592186286723 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically by\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-4},\\,\\,\\,y=2{t}^{2},\\,t\\ge 2.\n$$" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286723 1113 #uuid "4c02115b-ee53-598f-8c94-ffd8d53a4af5" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286723 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for ${t}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-4}\\,⇒\\,{t}^{2}={x}^{2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${t}^{2}={x}^{2}+4$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny=2({x}^{2}+4)=2{x}^{2}+8\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=2{x}^{2}+8.$\n\nFinally, since $t\\ge 2.$ and $x=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-4},$ we must have $x\\ge 0.$\n\nSo, the complete Cartesian equation is\n\n$$\ny=2{x}^{2}+8,\\,x\\ge 0.\n$$" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286725 13194139534407 true] [17592186286724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286726 13194139534407 true] [17592186286724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286727 13194139534407 true] [17592186286724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286728 13194139534407 true] [17592186286724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286729 13194139534407 true] [17592186286724 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534407 true] [17592186286724 1041 "selection" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286724 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286729 13194139534407 true] [17592186286724 1110 #uuid "e2daac1a-a539-562c-a441-e34cba65c3ad" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286725 1034 "y=4{x}^{2}-16,\\,x\\ge 0" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286725 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534407 true] [17592186286725 1111 #uuid "1ce20d2b-0525-5efb-94e4-e61d5a9b0a1c" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286726 1034 "y=2{x}^{2}+4,\\,x\\ge 0" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286726 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534407 true] [17592186286726 1111 #uuid "22f0f42c-a010-5832-8b66-a14e02e4928b" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286727 1034 "y=2{x}^{2}-8,\\,x\\ge 0" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286727 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534407 true] [17592186286727 1111 #uuid "434b7306-a7ea-510b-a7ee-4f88c52c66f5" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286728 1034 "y=4{x}^{2}+8,\\,x\\ge 0" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286728 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534407 true] [17592186286728 1111 #uuid "d369897d-2ac4-50d0-9a2b-2c7999cbd262" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286729 1034 "y=2{x}^{2}+8,\\,x\\ge 0" 13194139534407 true] [17592186286729 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534407 true] [17592186286729 1111 #uuid "9a52558f-8f1c-5b00-8ba5-3d37